<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="50–60 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>Adverbs of manner <em>choose what the description points at</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Show the quality of a person or thing, or show how an action happens: <span class="ex">The instructions are clear. The coordinator explained them clearly. The volunteers worked hard, and they moved the fragile boxes carefully.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">50–60 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">adjective · manner adverb</span>
    <span class="tag">form · meaning · placement</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Find whether a description points at an entity or an action.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Separate linking complements from manner descriptions.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Control spelling, changed meanings, and neutral placement.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Give a fictional observation briefing with natural rhythm.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can choose whether a description belongs to a person, thing, state, or action; form common manner adverbs; distinguish <span class="ex">well, fast, hard, late, hardly</span>, and <span class="ex">lately</span>; place a manner adverb naturally; and use sentence stress to make the intended contrast clear.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a comparative, future-reference present form, and frequency-adverb position.">
    <h3>Three checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use the comparison, future condition, and repeated-frequency context.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier lesson choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="slower">slower</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="slowest">slowest</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="arrives">arrives</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="will arrive">will arrive</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="always">always</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="yesterday">yesterday</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The office printer takes six minutes, but the other printer takes two: The office printer is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="slower" data-hint="Two printers are compared on speed, so use the comparative slower." data-fix="The office printer is slower than the other printer." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> than the other printer.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The key delivery is still an open future condition: If the key <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="arrives" data-hint="The core future condition uses present arrives, not will arrive." data-fix="If the key arrives, call Maya." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>, call Maya.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The coordinator checks every safety note without exception: She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="always" data-hint="Always goes before the main verb checks in this repeated routine." data-fix="She always checks every safety note." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> checks every safety note.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice where each description points</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Harbor workshop setup note</h3>
    <p><b>A quality of an entity:</b> <span class="ex">The instructions are clear. The room is quiet. The new volunteer is careful.</span></p>
    <p><b>The manner of an action:</b> <span class="ex">Maya explained the instructions clearly. The team worked quietly. The volunteer opened each box carefully.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which words point at instructions, a room, or a person?</li>
      <li>Which words point at explaining, working, or opening?</li>
      <li>Does every manner adverb have to end in <span class="ex">-ly</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated noun and subject qualities from clear, quiet, and careful ways of acting.">
    <h3>Discovery check: identify the description’s job</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Description job choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="entity quality">entity quality</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="action manner">action manner</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>In <span class="ex">a quiet room</span>, <span class="ex">quiet</span> describes the room, so it gives an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="entity quality" data-hint="Quiet points directly at the noun room." data-fix="Quiet gives an entity quality in a quiet room." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>In <span class="ex">The team worked quietly</span>, <span class="ex">quietly</span> answers how the team worked, so it gives an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="action manner" data-hint="Quietly describes the way the working happened." data-fix="Quietly gives action manner in The team worked quietly." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>In <span class="ex">The instructions sound clear</span>, <span class="ex">clear</span> evaluates the instructions, so it gives an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="entity quality" data-hint="Sound links the instructions to the quality clear in this sentence." data-fix="Clear gives an entity quality in The instructions sound clear." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>In <span class="ex">Maya spoke clearly</span>, <span class="ex">clearly</span> describes the speaking, so it gives an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="action manner" data-hint="Clearly answers how Maya spoke." data-fix="Clearly gives action manner in Maya spoke clearly." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>In <span class="ex">The plan looks good</span>, <span class="ex">good</span> evaluates the plan, so it gives an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="entity quality" data-hint="Looks links the plan to the evaluation good here." data-fix="Good gives an entity quality in The plan looks good." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>In <span class="ex">The team performed well</span>, <span class="ex">well</span> evaluates how the performance happened, so it gives an <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="action manner" data-hint="Well is the manner form related to good when it describes performance." data-fix="Well gives action manner in The team performed well." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: choose the target before the form</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A manner adverb describes how an action is performed or how an event happens. An adjective can describe a noun directly or complete a linking meaning after verbs such as <span class="ex">be, seem, become, look, sound, feel, smell</span>, and <span class="ex">taste</span>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>target</th><th>use</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>noun</td><td>adjective before the noun</td><td><span class="ex">a careful volunteer</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>subject quality or state</td><td>adjective after a linking meaning</td><td><span class="ex">The volunteer seems careful.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>action or event</td><td>manner adverb</td><td><span class="ex">The volunteer opened the box carefully.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Do not decide from the verb alone. Meaning controls the pattern. <span class="ex">The fabric feels soft</span> links fabric to a quality, but <span class="ex">Maya felt the edge carefully</span> uses <span class="ex">felt</span> as an action and <span class="ex">carefully</span> describes that action.</p>

  <h2>Build common manner forms accurately</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Many manner adverbs use an adjective plus <span class="ex">-ly</span>, but spelling depends on the adjective’s ending. Learn the useful pattern and the complete word together.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>adjective ending</th><th>usual change</th><th>examples</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>most forms</td><td>add <span class="ex">-ly</span></td><td><span class="ex">careful → carefully; polite → politely</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>consonant + <span class="ex">y</span></td><td>change <span class="ex">y</span> to <span class="ex">i</span>, then add <span class="ex">-ly</span></td><td><span class="ex">easy → easily; happy → happily</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>consonant + <span class="ex">le</span></td><td>drop final <span class="ex">e</span>, then add <span class="ex">y</span></td><td><span class="ex">gentle → gently; simple → simply</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>many forms ending in <span class="ex">-ic</span></td><td>add <span class="ex">-ally</span></td><td><span class="ex">basic → basically; automatic → automatically</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Some useful spellings must be stored separately, including <span class="ex">true → truly</span> and <span class="ex">full → fully</span>. A spelling pattern is a strong guide, not permission to invent every possible <span class="ex">-ly</span> word.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You formed regular, consonant-y, consonant-le, and -ic manner adverbs accurately.">
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the complete manner form</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Manner form choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="carefully">carefully</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="carefuly">carefuly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="easily">easily</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="easyly">easyly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="gently">gently</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="gentlely">gentlely</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="automatically">automatically</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="automaticly">automaticly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="happily">happily</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="happyly">happyly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="politely">politely</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="polity">polity</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The boxes contain glass, so the volunteer checks each label <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="carefully" data-hint="Careful takes the usual -ly ending, with both l letters represented in carefully." data-fix="The volunteer checks each label carefully." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The signs are large and numbered, so visitors find the entrance <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="easily" data-hint="Consonant plus y changes to i before -ly: easy becomes easily." data-fix="Visitors find the entrance easily." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The device is fragile, so Maya places it on the table <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="gently" data-hint="Gentle drops final e and adds y: gently." data-fix="Maya places the device on the table gently." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>A sensor controls the door, so it closes <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="automatically" data-hint="Many adjectives ending in -ic add -ally: automatic becomes automatically." data-fix="The door closes automatically." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The fictional team celebrates the successful setup with smiles: They pose for the photo <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="happily" data-hint="Consonant plus y changes to i before -ly: happy becomes happily." data-fix="They pose for the photo happily." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The visitor asks for help using a respectful tone: She speaks <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="politely" data-hint="Polite keeps its final e before -ly: politely." data-fix="She speaks politely to the volunteer." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> to the volunteer.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Keep changed forms and changed meanings apart</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>intended meaning</th><th>form</th><th>contrast</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>in a good way</td><td><span class="ex">well</span></td><td><span class="ex">The team performed well.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>at high speed</td><td><span class="ex">fast</span></td><td>not <span class="ex">fastly</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>with great effort</td><td><span class="ex">hard</span></td><td><span class="ex">hardly</span> means almost not</td></tr>
      <tr><td>after the expected time</td><td><span class="ex">late</span></td><td><span class="ex">lately</span> means recently</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">Well</span> is the changed manner form related to <span class="ex">good</span>. It can also be an adjective meaning healthy: <span class="ex">Maya performed well</span>, but <span class="ex">Maya is well again</span>.</p>
  <p class="note-line"><span class="ex">Fast, hard</span>, and <span class="ex">late</span> are often called flat adverbs because the adjective and adverb share a form. Adding <span class="ex">-ly</span> either creates a different meaning or, with <span class="ex">fastly</span>, does not create the standard manner word.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished good performance, speed, effort, delay, almost-not meaning, and recent time.">
    <h3>Drill 2: choose the intended form and meaning</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Changed form and meaning choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="well">well</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="good">good</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fast">fast</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fastly">fastly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hard">hard</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hardly">hardly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="late">late</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="lately">lately</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The evaluator gives the fictional team a high score for its performance: The team performed <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="well" data-hint="Use the changed manner form well for performance in a good way." data-fix="The team performed well." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The cart crossed the room in five seconds, so it moved <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="fast" data-hint="Fast is the standard manner form for high speed; fastly is not." data-fix="The cart moved fast." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The volunteers used great effort for the entire morning: They worked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hard" data-hint="Hard means with great effort in this context." data-fix="They worked hard all morning." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> all morning.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The bus was scheduled for 8:00 but arrived at 8:20: It arrived <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="late" data-hint="Late means after the expected time." data-fix="The bus arrived late." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The speaker’s microphone was almost silent: The audience could <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hardly" data-hint="Hardly means almost not, which matches almost no sound." data-fix="The audience could hardly hear the speaker." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> hear the speaker.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>In recent weeks, the public room has had more bookings: It has been busier <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="lately" data-hint="Lately means recently, not after the expected time." data-fix="It has been busier lately." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Place the manner without breaking the action</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>The safest neutral pattern puts a manner adverb after the verb when there is no object, or after a short direct object. Keep the verb and its short object together.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>action shape</th><th>neutral placement</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>verb with no object</td><td>after the verb</td><td><span class="ex">Maya spoke clearly.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>verb plus short object</td><td>after the object</td><td><span class="ex">Maya explained the rule clearly.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td>frequency plus manner</td><td>frequency before the main verb; manner after the action</td><td><span class="ex">Maya always checks the list carefully.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>A manner adverb can also appear before the main verb: <span class="ex">Maya carefully opened the fragile package</span>. This often foregrounds the way she performed the whole action. End position remains the safest neutral choice: <span class="ex">Maya opened the fragile package carefully</span>.</p>
  <p class="note-line">Do not turn a useful core pattern into an absolute rule. Preverb placement is normal. What the core pattern avoids is splitting a verb from a short direct object: prefer <span class="ex">explain the route clearly</span> to <span class="ex">explain clearly the route</span>.</p>

  <h3>Linking meaning or action meaning?</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>linking meaning and adjective</th><th>action meaning and manner adverb</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">The instructions sound clear.</span></td><td><span class="ex">Maya spoke clearly.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">The fabric feels soft.</span></td><td><span class="ex">Maya felt the edge carefully.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">Maya looks calm.</span></td><td><span class="ex">Maya looked carefully at the diagram.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You controlled neutral end position, object order, frequency plus manner, linking complements, action meaning, and purposeful preverb placement.">
    <h3>Drill 3: choose meaning and placement</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Meaning and placement choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="spoke clearly">spoke clearly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="clearly spoke">clearly spoke</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="explained the route clearly">explained the route clearly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="explained clearly the route">explained clearly the route</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="always checks the list carefully">always checks the list carefully</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="checks always carefully the list">checks always carefully the list</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="clear">clear</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="clearly">clearly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="carefully">carefully</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="careful">careful</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="carefully opened">carefully opened</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="opened careful">opened careful</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>No object follows the verb, and the event note uses neutral end placement: The coordinator <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="spoke clearly" data-hint="With no object, neutral manner placement follows the verb: spoke clearly." data-fix="The coordinator spoke clearly." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Keep the short object <span class="ex">the route</span> beside its verb, then add the manner: Maya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="explained the route clearly" data-hint="The neutral core order is verb plus object plus manner adverb." data-fix="Maya explained the route clearly." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>This is an exception-free routine performed with care: Maya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="always checks the list carefully" data-hint="Always goes before checks, while carefully follows the object the list." data-fix="Maya always checks the list carefully." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The listener evaluates the quality of the instructions, not an action by the instructions: They sound <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="clear" data-hint="Sound links instructions to the adjective clear in this meaning." data-fix="The instructions sound clear." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Maya actively examines the diagram and uses care while looking: She looked <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="carefully" data-hint="Looked is an action before at the diagram, so carefully describes how she looked." data-fix="She looked carefully at the diagram." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at the diagram.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The writer wants the care to frame the whole fragile-package action before naming it: Maya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="carefully opened" data-hint="The requested foregrounded manner uses carefully before the main verb opened." data-fix="Maya carefully opened the fragile package." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the fragile package.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use natural U.S. forms without inventing a false ban</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>In informal U.S. English, some flat adverbs are common in fixed expressions and casual speech: <span class="ex">Drive safe. Go slow. Hold tight.</span> Signs often say <span class="ex">GO SLOW</span>. In neutral careful speech and writing, <span class="ex">drive safely</span> and <span class="ex">walk slowly</span> are reliable choices.</p>
  <p class="note-line">Do not mark every common flat form as impossible. For this lesson’s controlled tasks, use the requested neutral form. In real conversation, first identify whether the form is a recognized expression, a register choice, or an actual error.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: attach <span class="ex">-ly</span> lightly and stress the new contrast</h3>
    <p>The <span class="ex">-ly</span> ending is normally an unstressed part of the word, pronounced /li/. Keep the main word stress: <span class="ex"><strong>CARE</strong>fully /ˈkɛrfəli/, <strong>QUICK</strong>ly /ˈkwɪkli/, <strong>EA</strong>sily /ˈizəli/, auto<strong>MAT</strong>ically /ˌɔtəˈmæɾɪkli/</span>.</p>
    <p>In a neutral answer to <span class="ex">How did Maya explain it?</span>, the new manner can carry the strongest sentence stress: <span class="ex">She explained it <strong>CLEAR</strong>ly.</span> Contrast can move the beat: <span class="ex">She explained the <strong>ROUTE</strong> clearly, not the schedule.</span></p>
    <p>Say the adverb as one word without a pause before <span class="ex">-ly</span>. In connected speech, keep the verb and object as one group, then attach the end-position manner: <span class="ex">explained-the-route <strong>CLEAR</strong>ly</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read adjective complement, neutral manner, hard-hardly, late-lately, flat U.S. form, and preverb-manner listening check">
    <h2>Listen for target, meaning, and position</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p class="note-line"><b>Tutor-read listening:</b> Keep the transcript closed. Read each item once naturally and once more after the learner chooses. The learner should use the complete message, not one isolated ending.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You heard a linking complement, neutral manner, effort, almost-not meaning, U.S. flat usage, and foregrounded preverb manner.">
      <h3>Six listening decisions</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The instructions have a clear quality." data-hint="After sound, clear evaluates the instructions in this message." data-fix="The instructions have a clear quality."><p class="quiz-question">1. What does the first message evaluate?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The instructions have a clear quality.">The instructions have a clear quality.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The instructions perform an action clearly.">The instructions perform an action clearly.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The coordinator speaks at a high volume.">The coordinator speaks at a high volume.</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="after the short object them" data-hint="Listen for explained them clearly: the object remains beside the verb." data-fix="Clearly comes after the short object them."><p class="quiz-question">2. Where does <span class="ex">clearly</span> appear in the second message?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="after the short object them">after the short object them</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="between explained and them">between explained and them</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="before the subject coordinator">before the subject coordinator</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="great effort" data-hint="Hard, without -ly, describes the volunteer’s effort." data-fix="Worked hard means worked with great effort."><p class="quiz-question">3. What does <span class="ex">worked hard</span> mean in the third message?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="great effort">great effort</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="almost no work">almost no work</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="recent work">recent work</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="almost could not hear" data-hint="Hardly means almost not in the fourth message." data-fix="Could hardly hear means almost could not hear."><p class="quiz-question">4. What does the fourth message say about hearing the announcement?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="almost could not hear">almost could not hear</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="heard it with great effort from the speaker">heard it with great effort from the speaker</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="heard it recently">heard it recently</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="an informal U.S. instruction to reduce speed" data-hint="Go slow is a common flat-adverb instruction in informal U.S. usage." data-fix="Go slow is an informal U.S. instruction to reduce speed."><p class="quiz-question">5. How should the fifth message be understood?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an informal U.S. instruction to reduce speed">an informal U.S. instruction to reduce speed</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="an impossible English form with no meaning">an impossible English form with no meaning</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a request to arrive late">a request to arrive late</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="before opened, foregrounding care across the action" data-hint="The sixth message begins the action phrase with carefully opened." data-fix="Carefully appears before opened and foregrounds care across the action."><p class="quiz-question">6. Where is the manner adverb in the sixth message, and what does it foreground?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="before opened, foregrounding care across the action">before opened, foregrounding care across the action</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="after package, describing only the package">after package, describing only the package</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="after Maya, describing Maya’s permanent character">after Maya, describing Maya’s permanent character</button></div></div>
